    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full `mvn test` build succeeded. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a **per-city** sequence.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the generator, now:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `city`\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- `NNNN` = 4-digit sequence = one more than the owners already in that city (counted via `findAll()` filtered by `city.equalsIgnoreCase(...)`, following the repo's established in-memory counting idiom, and excluding the not-yet-persisted new owner as `AssignNamesakeCount` does)\n\n**Derived value \u2014 `membershipNumber`** (`OwnerMapper`, format `<customerCode>-M<YY>`) embeds the customerCode verbatim, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`). No logic change was needed there.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` schema descriptions and examples to reflect the new format.\n\n**Tests:** `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 the full suite is green, including `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, which asserts the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` pattern.",
